# docs/style.md 1.2 (rule-function-names): every function and method is
# CamelCase, with one exception, the lower-case libc and manpage names of the
# thin syscall wrappers: functions of namespace dcfs::syscalls defined in
# dcfs/syscalls.h, syscalls_backing.{h,cc}, syscalls_process.{h,cc} and
# syscalls.cc (or, for this rule's good fixture, standing in for one). Step
# 25.41 moves the exception to the members of the Syscalls interface and its
# implementations. clang-tidy cannot scope an exception to a namespace, so
# readability-identifier-naming does not check functions (.clang-tidy) and
# this matcher does. Not reported: the names the language gives (constructors,
# destructors, conversion functions, operators, main), implicit functions,
# instantiations of templates, an override of a virtual (the base is checked;
# an external one such as what() is not ours to name), what gtest's
# INSTANTIATE_TEST_SUITE_P expands to, the link-time fakes the linker names
# (__wrap_x, __real_x), and an accessor in Google's sense (russ, 2026-10-19:
# "Google's style guide stands. Lowerecase getters and setters are
# permitted."): a non-static member function with no parameter that does not
# return void (a getter), or named set_x with one parameter (a setter). The
# shape is all clang-query can see, so a non-accessor of that shape passes.
# An extern "C" declaration without a body names a C function.
# A function whose name begins with a lower-case letter or an underscore,
# outside the exception.
match functionDecl(isExpansionInFileMatching("(^|/)(dcfs|tools|bench|test/qemu/guest)/"), matchesName("(^|::)[a-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*$"), unless(anyOf(isImplicit(), isMain(), matchesName("(^|::)__(wrap|real)_"), cxxMethodDecl(isOverride()), cxxMethodDecl(unless(isStaticStorageClass()), anyOf(allOf(parameterCountIs(0), unless(returns(voidType()))), allOf(matchesName("(^|::)set_[a-z0-9_]*$"), parameterCountIs(1)))), isExpandedFromMacro("INSTANTIATE_TEST_SUITE_P"), allOf(isExternC(), unless(isDefinition())), cxxConstructorDecl(), cxxDestructorDecl(), cxxConversionDecl(), isTemplateInstantiation(), allOf(hasDeclContext(namespaceDecl(hasName("::dcfs::syscalls"))), isExpansionInFileMatching("(^|/)(dcfs/syscalls(_backing|_process)?[.](cc|h)|tools/style_matchers/function_names_good[.]cc)$"))))).bind("function_names")
